			]
		}
		{
			title: "Loot n' Plunder"
			x: -6.75d
			y: -1.75d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "An Experience All It's Own"
			description: [
				"&dIf you are finding yourself outpacing your equipment a bit too fast, Bandit, you can make a Plunderer's Vault Rock."
				""
				"&5Ye use it on a Vault Altar like a normal Vault Rock, and pay the price to turn it into a special Vault Crystal."
				""
				"&dThis one can't be modified further, but the Plunder modifier changes a few things. First off, you get almost no experience in the Vault. Small things might give a bit of XP, but nowhere even close to what you would normally get."
				""
				"&5It also boosts the loot ye can find. A bit more loot in the chests, and a bigger percentage of Vault Ores being in Mining POIs and rooms."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["2EC8B80AE1A271D5"]
			id: "731864D511892F56"
			tasks: [{
				id: "5274C8F1E84DE605"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:plunderer_pearl"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "24D05ED99D59BD14"
				type: "choice"
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				table_id: 5632731352558517809L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "A Good Crate"
			x: -9.75d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "For a Tough Battle"
			description: [
				"&dSo we'll eventually need some Tokens from these Scavenger Crates, Bandit, but for now they aren't required."
				""
				"&5Scavenger is the toughest for a solo User to complete. It's easier with some Assistants, but Power Users don't always have the luxury of other Power Users joining them."
				""
				"&dScav Crates tend to have the best loot chances in them. Brazier crates have the worst, relatively, because of how easy Brazier is to complete."
				""
				"&5Ya can just ignore most of the mobs in em. Don't get ya a lot of souls that way but..."
			]
			hide_dependency_lines: true
			dependencies: ["1881243BF68F0FAC"]
			id: "1AA95F28498D1C57"
			tasks: [{
				id: "590F16B5A7F2DCAB"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:vault_crate_scavenger"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "1AEF77A9FC59D468"
				type: "choice"
				exclude_from_claim_all: true
				table_id: 2245246540467579945L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Creating The Divine Paradox"
			x: -2.75d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "Build A Vault Now Open!"
			description: [
				"&dOkay, I was waiting for this to become open to you, Bandit. It's going to be another way for us to crack the FOPGame Server open more. It's called The Divine Paradox."
				""
				"&5This is a special Vault that is tied in with the four Vault Gods. Ye start by making an Architect Vault Rock and paying the cost of it, as usual."
				""
				"&dDon't head in yet, though, Bandit. Few things need explaining first. Like the Architect vault crystal has no objective or loot. It's specifically for \"Creating\" your Divine Paradox vault."
				""
				"&5See, when ye first activate yer Divine Vault, it's... empty. Empty except for the entrance room. You 'build' out your Divine Paradox by purchasing connecting rooms with Vault Gold and materials."
				""
				"&dSome rooms require a certain amount of a certain Vault God's reputation as well to purchase."
			]
			dependencies: ["1799D40CDE8D8F82"]
			id: "72FAD25A9DA18C65"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7E27744A43339606"
				type: "item"
				item: "the_vault:crystal_seal_ordinator_build"
			}]
			rewards: [{
				id: "44C2A80D872E7A10"
				type: "choice"
				table_id: 2640422954496342337L
			}]
		}
		{
			title: "Running the Divine Paradox"
			x: -0.75d
			y: 0.25d
			shape: "pentagon"
			subtitle: "A Limited Time Deal"
			description: [
				"&dSo, you know how to build out your Divine Paradox, Bandit. Now we'll explain how you run it."
				""
				"&5The FOP have put a cooldown on running one, though. Ye can only run yer Divine Paradox once every 20 real life hours."
				""
				"&dIn in-game time that's about once every 60 days."
				""
				"&5But it's understandable. When you've unlocked a lot of special rooms, the Divine Paradox ends up being so lucrative ye run them as much as possible."
				""
				"&dThey have to special generate these vaults, which left a lot of... lesser worlds untouched until they put a cooldown."
				""
				"&5But ye, to run a Paradox Vault, ye just need to make and pay for a Paradox's Vault Rock."
			]
			dependencies: ["72FAD25A9DA18C65"]
			id: "391277708CA4B52A"
